 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"T-shirt Order Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a T-shirt order form used for?\", \"a\": \"A T-shirt order form collects what each buyer wants printed: the style, color, size and quantity, along with their name and how they pay. Organizers use it to total every size for the printer before a print run.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make a T-shirt order form online?\", \"a\": \"List the shirts and their prices, then decide when orders close. Describe that to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> and it builds a T-shirt order form that takes payment and keeps a running count per size.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I add names and numbers to a shirt order form template?\", \"a\": \"Give each shirt line a text field for the name on the back and a number field capped at two digits. Put the upcharge next to each field, where buyers can watch the line total change before they pay. Ask for names in capitals, spelled exactly as they should print.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I use a T-shirt order form for a fundraiser?\", \"a\": \"Price each shirt at the printer's cost plus the amount each sale should raise, and price the larger sizes from their own, higher cost. Say on the form what the money pays for. Check the orders table halfway to the close date to see whether the run will reach the printer's minimum.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I count sizes from T-shirt order forms?\", \"a\": \"Count by style and color first, then by size within each group. The printer needs a separate total for every combination, such as 12 navy adult mediums. On paper that means one tally sheet per color. An online form that saves each order as a row adds up each combination for you once the form shuts.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a school T-shirt order form include?\", \"a\": \"Ask for the student's name and homeroom, a youth or adult size, and the quantity. Show the price and the date orders close. A good T-shirt order form template for schools also names a contact for size swaps after delivery.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make an editable T-shirt order form template?\", \"a\": \"Save the layout as a Word document, not a PDF or an image, and next year's prices and colors take a minute to change. An online form is editable too: change a price or add a color, and the next buyer sees it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a merchandise order form?\", \"a\": \"A merchandise order form covers more than shirts, such as hoodies, hats and tote bags, each with its own sizes or colors. Bands and clubs use one to take orders before printing. For goods that are not printed to order, a general order form fits better.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a shirt order form include spare shirts for size swaps?\", \"a\": \"Yes, for most group orders. Add a few spares in the sizes that sell best and record them as one order from the organizer, which puts them in the printer's count. A buyer who picked the wrong size can then swap on handout day instead of waiting for another print run.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are T-shirt order forms free?\", \"a\": \"Printable T-shirt order forms are free on many template sites. Building and publishing one in Emergent costs nothing on the free tier. When the shirt comes with a race entry, ask for the size on the <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/registration-form'>registration form</a> instead of a separate one.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}